  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electrical contractors and other wiring installation contractors (NAICS 238210) have seen lower federal spending so far in FY2026. Total obligations for FY2026 to date are $453M on 2,005 awards, with an average award size of $226K and obligations down 42.7% year over year. Obligations peaked at $945M in FY23 and then fell to $824M in FY24 and $791M in FY25 before the current total of $453M in FY26. Agencies across defense, veterans affairs, and diplomacy continue to drive most buying, while a relatively small set of vendors account for large shares of the current-year dollars. The market remains active in award count, but the drop in total obligations and average award size dynamics signal tighter spending compared with the last three fiscal years. Contractors bidding in this NAICS should expect a market where award volume persists but total dollars are meaningfully lower than recent peaks.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal spending for NAICS 238210 changed recently?",
        "body": "FY23 recorded the highest obligations at $945M. The Department of Defense and other buyers reduced pace after FY23, with obligations falling to $824M in FY24 and $791M in FY25, and then to $453M in FY26 to date. Obligations are down 42.7% year over year, even though award count remains at 2,005 and average award size is $226K."
      },
